    "result_text": "All 285 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field on the owner-creation response. When creating an owner, the response now includes `locality` set to `\"local\"` if the owner's city is the *single* most common city among owners existing at that time, otherwise `\"remote\"`.\n\nChanges made, following the same pattern as the existing derived fields (`namesakeCount`, `sharesHousehold`, etc.):\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema (plain string, not an enum, so MapStruct maps the model's `String` cleanly \u2014 an enum would fail `valueOf` on the lowercase values).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `locality` column field with getter/setter.\n- **Schema files** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added a `locality VARCHAR(20)` column.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 calls `owner.setLocality(locality(owner))` before saving, plus a new `locality(...)` helper that groups existing owners by (whitespace/case-normalized) city, finds the max frequency, and returns `\"local\"` only when exactly one city holds that max and it matches the new owner's city; `\"remote\"` otherwise (including no existing owners or a tie).\n\nThe computation runs before the owner is persisted, so it reflects only pre-existing owners \u2014 matching the spec's \"at that time.\"",
